  "ref": "JOS.10.24",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected at *the necks of these kings*: the single written *the* goes to the present article morpheme on הַמְּלָכִים, fronted to the phrase's left edge, not to the construct צַוְּארֵי as a supplied one. Rule 29 permits supplying a *the* on a construct noun only where no article morpheme is present, and rule 47 gives a written *the* to a present article before a supplied one; the demonstrative אֵלֶּה separately licenses *these*, so the article's only available realization is that *the*. The accepted alignment had s037 holding *the necks* and s038 `unrepresented`.",
    "The competing reading would treat the whole phrase as determined by the demonstrative and the *the* as supplied on the construct; it is rejected because it supplies a determiner while an article morpheme in the same chain goes unrendered.",
    "Unchanged elsewhere: rule 45's apodosis clause applies, the waw of וַיִּקְרָא carrying the frame's *that*; *Come near* keeps its head on the verb; and *the men of war* keeps the fronted *the* on the inner rectum's article with a supplied *the* on the outer construct *chiefs*."
  ]
